suppressed = true

That caused the cone to smoothly suppress.

This was legitimate live-data behavior.

Transition B — Surface expands

Later:

maxCones: 3 → undefined

That removed the three-cone restriction and allowed the full six-cone Surface representation.

That caused the second smooth transition.

Initially we suspected this was happening because surfaceActivated was changing.

It wasn't.

5. Discovery: surfaceActivated was not the problem

Instrumentation showed:

